      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِيفٌ</span></b>  [The <i>membranous fibres that grow at the
base of the branches of the palm-tree:</i>] the best
sort is the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ليف</span> of the cocoa-nut. (TA.) See
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرِيعٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِيفٌ</span> is used by Ibn-Mukbil as meaning
(assumed tropical:)  A she-camel's <i>tail.</i> (TA in arts. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شذب</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شمل</span>.)

